Third-party software used by this sample
========================================

This repository's own code is licensed under MIT-0 (see LICENSE), and the
repository doesn't vendor third-party source code. Building the gateway image,
with `docker compose up --build` or `cdk deploy`, downloads LiteLLM, NVIDIA
Switchyard, and the build tools below, and `cdk deploy` pushes the built image
to an Amazon ECR repository in your own AWS account. `npm ci` and the CI
workflow download the rest. Each component keeps its own license, as stated by
its upstream project.


LiteLLM
-------
Source:  the ghcr.io/berriai/litellm base image, pinned in
         docker/gateway/Dockerfile
License: MIT, except the content of its enterprise/ directory

The LiteLLM image also contains LiteLLM's enterprise code, as the
/app/enterprise directory and as the installed litellm-enterprise Python
package. That code is under the BerriAI Enterprise license, which is not an
open source license; using it in production requires a BerriAI Enterprise
subscription. This sample sets no LITELLM_LICENSE. Its profiles
(profiles/*/litellm.yaml) configure only the model list, the routing plugin,
timeouts, retries, and the master key, with no SSO, JWT authentication,
guardrails, audit logs, or database, and docker/gateway/start.sh only writes
the configuration files and starts the LiteLLM proxy.

The image is based on Wolfi and also contains operating system and Python
packages under their own licenses. These include GPL and LGPL operating system
packages (for example bash, busybox, glibc, readline, and xz), LGPL-3.0 Python
packages (psycopg and psycopg-binary), and Python packages with MPL-2.0 terms
(certifi, orjson, and tqdm).


